### Content (aligned with `det-app-primary-state.check.js`)

- **Purpose:** One visible lifecycle state per `[data-studio-workspace]` / `.studio-page`; counts `[data-studio-primary-state]` and `[class*="studio-state--"]`; PDCA plan/do/check/adjust.
- **Passing / failing signals:** Visibility rules (`hidden`, `aria-hidden`, `inert`, sub-4px), state vocabulary (empty/ready/running/completed/error), `metrics.primaryStateReport`.
- **Before:** Running + completed panels both visible (matches harness `det-app-primary-state-fail.html`).
- **After:** Completed panel `hidden` + `aria-hidden="true"`; active panel keeps `data-studio-primary-state`.
- **Evidence:** Remediation table, harness commands, link to `collectPrimaryStateReport` in the check module.

### Real KS classes in examples

`studio-page`, `doc-main`, `forge-card`, `card-label`, `text-cyan`, `font-display`, `forge-support`, `studio-state--running`, `studio-state--completed`, `data-studio-workspace`, `data-studio-primary-state` — same patterns as `det-app-primary-cta` and the defect fixture.

No Mermaid, no Fleet-specific profiles, check modules unchanged. After you run the `cp` above, the canonical handbook path will match the staging file.
